Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to restore ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200breturn something or someone to an \u200bearlier good \u200bcondition or \u200bposition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Restore work-life balance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about solving problems.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meditation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bact of giving \u200byour \u200battention to only one thing as a way of \u200bbecoming \u200bcalm and \u200brelaxed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Meditation can reduce your stress by calming your mind.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to minimize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make less", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Optimistic thinking helps you to cope with stressful situations and minimize the effect that stress can have on your body.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "optimism", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200bquality of being \u200bfull of \u200bhope and \u200ba \u200bbelief that something good will \u200bhappen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Research has shown that optimism or pessimism affects your quality of life. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to visualize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bform a \u200bpicture of someone or something in \u200byour \u200bmind, in \u200border to \u200bimagine it ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Concentration meditation is when you focus your attention on one thing, like an image you visualize or your breathing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to alter ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to \u200bchange something, usually \u200bslightly, or to \u200bcause the \u200bcharacteristics of something to \u200bchange", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are four ways that can help manage stress: avoid, alter, adapt or accept!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep your cool ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remain calm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You've got to keep your cool.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Relative Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use relative clauses to make your writing and speaking more detailed and sophisticated. A defining clause gives essential information about a noun. A non-defining clause gives additional information about a noun.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In relative clauses, you use <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things, <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with time and <span class=\"italic\">where</span> with places. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"underline\">Defining Clause</span>: <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">People <span class=\"strong\">who talk too much</span> annoy me a lot.</span><br/><br/>  Without the clause \u201cwho talk too much\u201d, the meaning of the sentence changes: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">People annoy me a lot. </span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"underline\">Non-defining Clause:</span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">My younger sister, <span class=\"strong\">who is really shy</span>, rarely speaks to anyone.</span><br/><br/>  Without the clause \u201cwho is really shy\u201d the main idea of the sentence stays the same. <br/> You need to use commas to keep the non-defining clause separate from the rest of the sentence.<br/><br/>  Look at some examples from the dialogue:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Research has shown that optimism or pessimism affects your quality of life. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Positive strategies which deal with stress help avoid negative consequences.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are different types of meditation techniques that can calm your mind and reduce your stress.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A solid social support network is a group of friends, family and peers who can help you through periods of stress.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are four ways to help manage stress: avoid, alter, adapt or accept!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Stress Management Tips", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Some workplace stress is normal. However, a lot of stress interferes with your workflow and influences your health, both physically and emotionally. Your ability to cope with it can make a big difference in your success at work.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are many things you can't control at your work, but there are things you can do. You don't need to make huge changes or rethink career ambitions. Try focus on the one things within your control: you.<br/><br/>  Read the following tips to manage workplace stress:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You should think positively.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You had better change your emotional response.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You ought to think about stress as a reaction to a problem, rather than the problem itself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You need to do things you enjoy and not feel guilty about it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should try meditation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You've got to keep your cool.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You need to maintain a strong social network.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, brainstorm all the ways you can reduce stress in your life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "On your own, choose 10 of your ideas and put them in order from most effective to least effective.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a short description for each tip.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Compare your list with your partner. Do you have many differences in your lists?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm ways to reduce stress.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a list of tips for reducing stress.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I put my list in order from most effective to least effective.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare my list with my partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}